{"lines": [{"text": "In nineteen ninety-nine, Google was for sale, for seven hundred fifty thousand dollars. And the buyer said no.", "start": 0.6, "end": 7.728, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "intro", "els": [{"e": "title", "a": "GOOGLE FOR $750,000?", "b": "…and the buyer said NO", "at": -1, "out": [2, 0]}, {"e": "check", "x": 640, "y": 620, "w": 720, "to": "Google", "amt": "$750,000", "at": -1, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "stamp", "txt": "DECLINED", "x": 640, "y": 640, "at": 0.55, "col": "red", "sz": 100, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "obj", "k": "samyell", "x": 1400, "y": 640, "w": 440, "at": -1, "out": [1, 0]}], "bg": "sky", "mood": "tense"}, "afx": null, "words": [["In", 0.087, 0.162], ["nineteen", 0.163, 0.537], ["ninety-nine", 0.537, 1.362], ["Google", 1.625, 2.087], ["was", 2.1, 2.275], ["for", 2.275, 2.438], ["sale", 2.45, 3.0], ["for", 3.263, 3.413], ["seven", 3.413, 3.712], ["hundred", 3.712, 3.95], ["fifty", 3.962, 4.338], ["thousand", 4.338, 4.75], ["dollars", 4.75, 5.312], ["And", 5.725, 5.775], ["the", 5.775, 5.85], ["buyer", 5.862, 6.188], ["said", 6.188, 6.45], ["no", 6.45, 6.763]]}, {"text": "Today, Google's parent company is worth more than three trillion dollars.", "start": 8.208, "end": 13.272, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "intro", "els": [{"e": "thennow", "then": "$750K", "now": "$3.6 TRILLION", "at": 0.1, "end": 0.8, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Today", 0.1, 0.45], ["Google's", 0.725, 1.062], ["parent", 1.062, 1.387], ["company", 1.387, 1.862], ["is", 2.275, 2.4], ["worth", 2.4, 2.6], ["more", 2.612, 2.9], ["than", 2.9, 3.062], ["three", 3.075, 3.625], ["trillion", 3.638, 4.112], ["dollars", 4.112, 4.7]]}, {"text": "It's not the only time someone said no to a fortune. A record label turned down the Beatles. Blockbuster laughed at Netflix.", "start": 13.752, "end": 22.2, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "intro", "els": [{"e": "vinyl", "x": 520, "y": 600, "r": 230, "label": "DECCA?", "at": 0.03, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "env", "x": 1380, "y": 600, "w": 520, "at": 0.45, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "stamp", "txt": "NO", "x": 520, "y": 600, "at": 0.3, "col": "red", "sz": 90, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "stamp", "txt": "NO", "x": 1380, "y": 600, "at": 0.8, "col": "red", "sz": 90, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["It's", 0.1, 0.188], ["not", 0.188, 0.338], ["the", 0.338, 0.425], ["only", 0.438, 0.688], ["time", 0.688, 0.988], ["someone", 1.0, 1.375], ["said", 1.387, 1.837], ["no", 2.112, 2.512], ["to", 2.525, 2.7], ["a", 2.712, 2.762], ["fortune", 2.763, 3.312], ["A", 3.712, 3.762], ["record", 3.775, 4.125], ["label", 4.138, 4.588], ["turned", 4.713, 5.025], ["down", 5.025, 5.238], ["the", 5.237, 5.3], ["Beatles", 5.3, 5.875], ["Blockbuster", 6.3, 6.862], ["laughed", 6.862, 7.312], ["at", 7.312, 7.388], ["Netflix", 7.388, 8.1]]}, {"text": "These are six times someone said no to a fortune, counted down to the most expensive no in history.", "start": 22.68, "end": 29.496, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "intro", "els": [{"e": "tx", "txt": "THEY SAID NO TO A FORTUNE", "x": 960, "y": 300, "size": 86, "at": 0, "col": "gold", "out": [2, 0.99]}, {"e": "ladder", "n": 6, "at": 0.2, "out": [2, 0.99]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["These", 0.1, 0.225], ["are", 0.225, 0.312], ["six", 0.325, 0.625], ["times", 0.625, 0.938], ["someone", 0.938, 1.3], ["said", 1.312, 1.762], ["no", 2.038, 2.513], ["to", 2.6, 2.788], ["a", 2.8, 2.862], ["fortune", 2.875, 3.45], ["counted", 3.812, 4.1], ["down", 4.1, 4.375], ["to", 4.375, 4.438], ["the", 4.438, 4.513], ["most", 4.525, 4.838], ["expensive", 4.85, 5.55], ["no", 5.55, 5.812], ["in", 5.812, 5.875], ["history", 5.888, 6.463]]}, {"text": "And one of them wasn't a mistake at all. Stay to the end, and you'll see why.", "start": 29.976, "end": 34.632, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "intro", "els": [{"e": "ladderhi", "x": 1290, "green": true, "txt": "not a mistake?", "at": 0.1, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["And", 0.1, 0.2], ["one", 0.2, 0.35], ["of", 0.35, 0.425], ["them", 0.425, 0.637], ["wasn't", 0.738, 1.05], ["a", 1.05, 1.075], ["mistake", 1.075, 1.475], ["at", 1.475, 1.538], ["all", 1.538, 1.825], ["Stay", 2.212, 2.4], ["to", 2.4, 2.475], ["the", 2.487, 2.587], ["end", 2.587, 3.0], ["and", 3.25, 3.325], ["you'll", 3.325, 3.463], ["see", 3.475, 3.825], ["why", 3.825, 4.275]]}, {"text": "Number six. London, New Year's Day, nineteen sixty-two.", "start": 35.112, "end": 39.576, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-3, 54, 2.4], "cam2": [-0.19, 51.55, 9], "chap": 6, "chapsub": "THE BAND NOBODY WANTED", "pins": [{"at": [-0.19, 51.55], "label": "Decca Studios", "col": "gold", "delay": 0.45}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Number", 0.1, 0.312], ["six", 0.325, 0.887], ["London", 1.288, 1.763], ["New", 2.05, 2.275], ["Year's", 2.275, 2.55], ["Day", 2.55, 2.85], ["nineteen", 2.862, 3.387], ["sixty-two", 3.388, 4.1]]}, {"text": "A young band from Liverpool drives down through the snow for an audition at Decca, one of the biggest record labels in Britain.", "start": 40.056, "end": 47.736, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "decca", "els": [{"e": "van", "x": 520, "y": 640, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "card", "x": 1340, "y": 330, "w": 620, "big": "Decca Records", "small": "audition · 1 January 1962", "at": 0.4, "col": "ink", "out": [1, 0]}], "bg": "sky", "mood": "calm"}, "afx": null, "words": [["A", 0.087, 0.125], ["young", 0.138, 0.487], ["band", 0.5, 0.887], ["from", 0.9, 1.125], ["Liverpool", 1.125, 1.688], ["drives", 1.7, 2.188], ["down", 2.188, 2.538], ["through", 2.55, 2.737], ["the", 2.75, 2.837], ["snow", 2.85, 3.438], ["for", 3.6, 3.775], ["an", 3.775, 3.85], ["audition", 3.85, 4.312], ["at", 4.312, 4.463], ["Decca", 4.475, 4.95], ["one", 5.487, 5.575], ["of", 5.575, 5.625], ["the", 5.625, 5.725], ["biggest", 5.737, 6.212], ["record", 6.225, 6.5], ["labels", 6.5, 6.838], ["in", 6.85, 6.925], ["Britain", 6.938, 7.3]]}, {"text": "They play fifteen songs in about an hour. Their name is the Beatles.", "start": 48.216, "end": 52.704, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "decca", "els": [{"e": "vinyl", "x": 560, "y": 600, "r": 240, "label": "15 SONGS", "at": 0, "out": [2, 0]}, {"e": "count", "x": 1340, "y": 440, "to": 15, "at": 0.1, "end": 0.45, "suf": " songs", "size": 120, "col": "gold", "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "🎸 The Beatles", "x": 1340, "y": 620, "size": 56, "at": 0.7, "bg": "blue", "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["They", 0.1, 0.175], ["play", 0.175, 0.425], ["fifteen", 0.425, 0.938], ["songs", 0.938, 1.375], ["in", 1.387, 1.488], ["about", 1.488, 1.713], ["an", 1.712, 1.775], ["hour", 1.775, 2.175], ["Their", 2.587, 2.712], ["name", 2.712, 3.075], ["is", 3.388, 3.475], ["the", 3.475, 3.562], ["Beatles", 3.562, 4.138]]}, {"text": "A few weeks later, the answer comes back. No. Decca signs another band instead, partly because they lived closer to London.", "start": 53.184, "end": 61.536, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "decca", "els": [{"e": "deal", "x": 1340, "y": 560, "press": 0.35, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "✍️ signed instead: Brian Poole and the Tremeloes", "x": 960, "y": 300, "size": 40, "at": 0.7, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["A", 0.087, 0.138], ["few", 0.138, 0.338], ["weeks", 0.338, 0.575], ["later", 0.588, 0.925], ["the", 1.175, 1.275], ["answer", 1.363, 1.663], ["comes", 1.663, 1.913], ["back", 1.913, 2.337], ["No.", 2.75, 3.05], ["Decca", 3.45, 3.663], ["signs", 3.663, 4.013], ["another", 4.013, 4.413], ["band", 4.412, 4.675], ["instead", 4.688, 5.225], ["partly", 5.65, 6.038], ["because", 6.037, 6.362], ["they", 6.362, 6.475], ["lived", 6.487, 6.825], ["closer", 6.825, 7.388], ["to", 7.388, 7.487], ["London", 7.5, 7.975]]}, {"text": "According to the Beatles' manager, Brian Epstein, he was told that guitar groups were on their way out.", "start": 62.016, "end": 67.704, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "decca", "els": [{"e": "letter", "x": 1340, "y": 290, "w": 700, "head": "DECCA RECORDS · LONDON", "body": "“Guitar groups are on their way out, Mr. Epstein.”", "at": 0.05, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "obj", "k": "samthink", "x": 520, "y": 640, "w": 380, "at": 0.1, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["According", 0.1, 0.412], ["to", 0.425, 0.487], ["the", 0.487, 0.6], ["Beatles'", 0.613, 0.938], ["manager", 0.938, 1.488], ["Brian", 1.75, 2.112], ["Epstein", 2.125, 2.688], ["he", 3.1, 3.15], ["was", 3.15, 3.288], ["told", 3.288, 3.6], ["that", 3.6, 3.725], ["guitar", 3.725, 4.125], ["groups", 4.138, 4.438], ["were", 4.438, 4.575], ["on", 4.575, 4.7], ["their", 4.7, 4.812], ["way", 4.812, 5.0], ["out", 5.013, 5.325]]}, {"text": "The executive who got the blame, Dick Rowe, always denied saying it. But the decision stuck to him for the rest of his life.", "start": 68.184, "end": 76.008, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "decca", "els": [{"e": "card", "x": 1340, "y": 320, "w": 640, "big": "Dick Rowe", "small": "always denied the quote", "at": 0.1, "col": "ink", "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "stamp", "txt": "BLAMED", "x": 1340, "y": 640, "at": 0.6, "col": "red", "sz": 80, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["The", 0.1, 0.138], ["executive", 0.138, 0.762], ["who", 0.762, 0.862], ["got", 0.863, 1.075], ["the", 1.075, 1.137], ["blame", 1.137, 1.663], ["Dick", 1.95, 2.188], ["Rowe", 2.2, 2.588], ["always", 2.888, 3.263], ["denied", 3.275, 3.75], ["saying", 3.75, 4.125], ["it", 4.138, 4.325], ["But", 4.725, 4.837], ["the", 4.838, 4.913], ["decision", 4.912, 5.45], ["stuck", 5.45, 5.763], ["to", 5.763, 5.875], ["him", 5.875, 6.175], ["for", 6.312, 6.438], ["the", 6.438, 6.5], ["rest", 6.5, 6.8], ["of", 6.8, 6.837], ["his", 6.838, 6.963], ["life", 6.975, 7.462]]}, {"text": "A few months later, the Beatles signed with a different label, and went on to become the best-selling band in music history.", "start": 76.488, "end": 83.52, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "decca", "els": [{"e": "vinyl", "x": 560, "y": 600, "r": 240, "label": "BEATLES", "gold": true, "at": 0.03, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "🏆 best-selling band in history", "x": 1340, "y": 520, "size": 48, "at": 0.6, "bg": "gold", "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["A", 0.087, 0.138], ["few", 0.138, 0.3], ["months", 0.312, 0.55], ["later", 0.55, 0.95], ["the", 1.337, 1.462], ["Beatles", 1.462, 1.912], ["signed", 1.925, 2.4], ["with", 2.4, 2.525], ["a", 2.525, 2.612], ["different", 2.688, 3.062], ["label", 3.075, 3.45], ["and", 3.888, 3.938], ["went", 3.938, 4.075], ["on", 4.075, 4.225], ["to", 4.225, 4.3], ["become", 4.3, 4.625], ["the", 4.625, 4.725], ["best-selling", 4.737, 5.45], ["band", 5.45, 5.838], ["in", 5.838, 5.913], ["music", 5.912, 6.2], ["history", 6.2, 6.688]]}, {"text": "Rowe did get one thing right afterwards. On a tip from George Harrison, he signed another guitar band: the Rolling Stones.", "start": 84.0, "end": 91.728, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "decca", "els": [{"e": "vinyl", "x": 560, "y": 600, "r": 220, "label": "DECCA", "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "💡 tip from George Harrison", "x": 1340, "y": 400, "size": 46, "at": 0.3, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "stamp", "txt": "SIGNED", "x": 1340, "y": 600, "at": 0.8, "col": "green", "sz": 90, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Rowe", 0.087, 0.188], ["did", 0.2, 0.325], ["get", 0.325, 0.5], ["one", 0.5, 0.812], ["thing", 0.812, 1.225], ["right", 1.45, 1.7], ["afterwards", 1.7, 2.4], ["On", 2.788, 2.863], ["a", 2.862, 2.912], ["tip", 2.913, 3.125], ["from", 3.138, 3.35], ["George", 3.362, 3.662], ["Harrison", 3.663, 4.138], ["he", 4.525, 4.613], ["signed", 4.612, 4.875], ["another", 4.875, 5.175], ["guitar", 5.175, 5.562], ["band", 5.562, 5.912], ["the", 6.338, 6.413], ["Rolling", 6.412, 6.762], ["Stones", 6.763, 7.35]]}, {"text": "Lesson one: experts can be wrong about what people will love.", "start": 92.208, "end": 96.0, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "decca", "els": [{"e": "obj", "k": "samthink", "x": 520, "y": 620, "w": 460, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "card", "x": 1300, "y": 380, "w": 760, "big": "Lesson #1", "small": "Experts can be wrong about what people will love.", "at": 0.2, "col": "gold", "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Lesson", 0.1, 0.425], ["one", 0.438, 0.7], ["experts", 1.212, 1.6], ["can", 1.613, 1.713], ["be", 1.712, 1.837], ["wrong", 1.837, 2.2], ["about", 2.2, 2.45], ["what", 2.45, 2.588], ["people", 2.6, 2.913], ["will", 2.913, 3.025], ["love", 3.025, 3.425]]}, {"text": "Number five. Rochester, New York, nineteen seventy-five.", "start": 96.48, "end": 101.208, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-98, 39, 1.0], "cam2": [-77.61, 43.16, 8], "chap": 5, "chapsub": "THE CAMERA THEY HID", "pins": [{"at": [-77.61, 43.16], "label": "Kodak", "col": "gold", "delay": 0.45}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Number", 0.1, 0.312], ["five", 0.325, 0.775], ["Rochester, New York", 1.188, 2.8], ["nineteen", 3.013, 3.55], ["seventy-five", 3.55, 4.35]]}, {"text": "Kodak ruled photography. It made money on almost every roll of film people bought.", "start": 101.688, "end": 107.04, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "kodak", "els": [{"e": "film", "x": 560, "y": 600, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "🎞️ film = Kodak's money machine", "x": 1340, "y": 420, "size": 46, "at": 0.4, "out": [1, 0]}], "bg": "sky", "mood": "calm"}, "afx": null, "words": [["Kodak", 0.087, 0.5], ["ruled", 0.512, 0.8], ["photography", 0.8, 1.525], ["It", 1.925, 1.975], ["made", 1.975, 2.15], ["money", 2.163, 2.525], ["on", 2.525, 2.625], ["almost", 2.625, 3.025], ["every", 3.163, 3.488], ["roll", 3.487, 3.887], ["of", 3.888, 3.963], ["film", 3.975, 4.287], ["people", 4.287, 4.575], ["bought", 4.575, 4.975]]}, {"text": "Then a twenty-four-year-old engineer named Steve Sasson built something strange: a camera with no film at all.", "start": 107.52, "end": 114.84, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "kodak", "els": [{"e": "camera", "x": 620, "y": 600, "w": 520, "at": 0, "out": [3, 0]}, {"e": "card", "x": 1340, "y": 330, "w": 620, "big": "Steve Sasson", "small": "Kodak engineer · age 24", "at": 0.35, "col": "ink", "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "stamp", "txt": "NO FILM", "x": 1340, "y": 640, "at": 0.8, "col": "red", "sz": 80, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Then", 0.1, 0.188], ["a", 0.188, 0.237], ["twenty-four-year-old", 0.237, 1.025], ["engineer", 1.025, 1.575], ["named", 1.812, 2.087], ["Steve", 2.087, 2.438], ["Sasson", 2.438, 2.987], ["built", 3.288, 3.5], ["something", 3.5, 3.938], ["strange", 3.95, 4.625], ["a", 5.125, 5.188], ["camera", 5.2, 5.737], ["with", 5.925, 6.087], ["no", 6.088, 6.338], ["film", 6.338, 6.613], ["at", 6.612, 6.675], ["all", 6.675, 6.938]]}, {"text": "It weighed about eight pounds, and took black-and-white pictures of just a hundred by a hundred pixels.", "start": 115.32, "end": 121.2, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "kodak", "els": [{"e": "camera", "x": 620, "y": 600, "w": 520, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pixels", "x": 1340, "y": 560, "w": 420, "at": 0.35, "end": 0.85, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "100 × 100 pixels", "x": 1340, "y": 830, "size": 44, "at": 0.7, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["It", 0.1, 0.188], ["weighed", 0.2, 0.363], ["about", 0.362, 0.625], ["eight", 0.637, 0.825], ["pounds", 0.825, 1.375], ["and", 1.387, 1.675], ["took", 1.837, 2.1], ["black-and-white", 2.112, 2.812], ["pictures", 2.812, 3.413], ["of", 3.525, 3.663], ["just", 3.663, 3.85], ["a", 3.85, 3.875], ["hundred", 3.875, 4.388], ["by", 4.388, 4.525], ["a", 4.525, 4.562], ["hundred", 4.575, 4.875], ["pixels", 4.875, 5.5]]}, {"text": "Each photo took twenty-three seconds to save, onto a cassette tape.", "start": 121.68, "end": 126.144, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "kodak", "els": [{"e": "camera", "x": 620, "y": 600, "w": 520, "rec": true, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "count", "x": 1340, "y": 460, "to": 23, "at": 0.1, "end": 0.8, "suf": " sec", "size": 140, "col": "gold", "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "📼 saved to cassette tape", "x": 1340, "y": 620, "size": 44, "at": 0.6, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Each", 0.087, 0.25], ["photo", 0.25, 0.613], ["took", 0.625, 0.85], ["twenty-three", 0.863, 1.462], ["seconds", 1.462, 1.95], ["to", 1.95, 2.038], ["save", 2.05, 2.575], ["onto", 3.013, 3.275], ["a", 3.288, 3.35], ["cassette", 3.362, 3.787], ["tape", 3.788, 4.1]]}, {"text": "Sasson showed it to Kodak's managers. They were convinced nobody would ever want to look at their photos on a TV screen.", "start": 126.624, "end": 133.8, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "kodak", "els": [{"e": "obj", "k": "samthink", "x": 520, "y": 640, "w": 380, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "letter", "x": 1340, "y": 300, "w": 700, "head": "KODAK MANAGEMENT · 1975", "body": "“No one would ever want to look at their pictures on a television set.”", "at": 0.15, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Sasson", 0.1, 0.525], ["showed", 0.525, 0.812], ["it", 0.825, 0.912], ["to", 0.912, 1.012], ["Kodak's", 1.025, 1.5], ["managers", 1.5, 2.175], ["They", 2.587, 2.637], ["were", 2.638, 2.725], ["convinced", 2.725, 3.25], ["nobody", 3.263, 3.838], ["would", 4.037, 4.225], ["ever", 4.325, 4.55], ["want", 4.562, 4.662], ["to", 4.662, 4.7], ["look", 4.7, 4.9], ["at", 4.9, 4.95], ["their", 4.963, 5.088], ["photos", 5.088, 5.738], ["on", 5.825, 5.925], ["a", 5.938, 5.975], ["TV", 5.975, 6.375], ["screen", 6.388, 6.812]]}, {"text": "And a camera without film threatened the film business that paid for everything. So Kodak didn't push it.", "start": 134.28, "end": 140.568, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "kodak", "els": [{"e": "deal", "x": 1340, "y": 560, "press": 0.45, "at": 0, "txt": "DIGITAL?", "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "film", "x": 560, "y": 600, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["And", 0.1, 0.175], ["a", 0.188, 0.237], ["camera", 0.25, 0.662], ["without", 0.662, 1.038], ["film", 1.05, 1.5], ["threatened", 1.587, 2.038], ["the", 2.038, 2.1], ["film", 2.1, 2.425], ["business", 2.438, 2.913], ["that", 2.925, 3.1], ["paid", 3.1, 3.488], ["for", 3.487, 3.662], ["everything", 3.663, 4.188], ["So", 4.588, 4.763], ["Kodak", 4.763, 5.275], ["didn't", 5.275, 5.488], ["push", 5.487, 5.75], ["it", 5.75, 5.912]]}, {"text": "Others did. Digital cameras took over, and then phones put a camera in almost every pocket.", "start": 141.048, "end": 147.384, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "kodak", "els": [{"e": "camera", "x": 560, "y": 600, "w": 420, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "obj", "k": "phone", "x": 1340, "y": 600, "w": 420, "at": 0.55, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "📷 → 📱", "x": 960, "y": 300, "size": 60, "at": 0.4, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Others", 0.1, 0.363], ["did", 0.362, 0.662], ["Digital", 1.038, 1.45], ["cameras", 1.45, 2.038], ["took", 2.188, 2.462], ["over", 2.475, 2.863], ["and", 3.312, 3.362], ["then", 3.362, 3.537], ["phones", 3.55, 4.013], ["put", 4.013, 4.163], ["a", 4.175, 4.225], ["camera", 4.225, 4.737], ["in", 4.75, 4.825], ["almost", 4.838, 5.213], ["every", 5.35, 5.537], ["pocket", 5.537, 6.0]]}, {"text": "In twenty twelve, Kodak, the company that invented the digital camera, filed for bankruptcy.", "start": 147.864, "end": 153.888, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "kodak", "els": [{"e": "chart", "kind": "crash", "x": 300, "y": 300, "w": 1320, "h": 520, "at": 0, "end": 0.6, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "stamp", "txt": "BANKRUPT", "x": 960, "y": 560, "at": 0.65, "col": "red", "sz": 110, "out": [1, 0]}], "cut": true, "mood": "tense"}, "afx": null, "words": [["In", 0.1, 0.188], ["twenty", 0.188, 0.463], ["twelve", 0.463, 0.975], ["Kodak", 1.175, 1.75], ["the", 1.975, 2.075], ["company", 2.075, 2.413], ["that", 2.413, 2.55], ["invented", 2.55, 3.012], ["the", 3.013, 3.125], ["digital", 3.188, 3.575], ["camera", 3.587, 4.1], ["filed", 4.487, 4.85], ["for", 4.85, 4.975], ["bankruptcy", 4.975, 5.675]]}, {"text": "Lesson two: if you don't replace your own product, someone else will.", "start": 154.368, "end": 158.856, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "kodak", "els": [{"e": "obj", "k": "samsad", "x": 520, "y": 620, "w": 460, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "card", "x": 1300, "y": 380, "w": 760, "big": "Lesson #2", "small": "If you don't replace your own product, someone else will.", "at": 0.2, "col": "gold", "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Lesson", 0.1, 0.45], ["two", 0.45, 0.863], ["if", 1.4, 1.525], ["you", 1.525, 1.6], ["don't", 1.6, 1.825], ["replace", 1.825, 2.188], ["your", 2.188, 2.3], ["own", 2.3, 2.462], ["product", 2.462, 2.875], ["someone", 3.263, 3.55], ["else", 3.55, 3.775], ["will", 3.775, 4.112]]}, {"text": "Number four. Dallas, Texas, the year two thousand.", "start": 159.336, "end": 163.536, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-98, 39, 1.0], "cam2": [-96.8, 32.78, 8], "chap": 4, "chapsub": "THE DEAL THEY LAUGHED AT", "pins": [{"at": [-96.8, 32.78], "label": "Blockbuster HQ", "col": "gold", "delay": 0.45}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Number", 0.1, 0.325], ["four", 0.325, 0.7], ["Dallas, Texas", 1.1, 2.312], ["the", 2.337, 2.425], ["year", 2.425, 2.887], ["two", 3.05, 3.25], ["thousand", 3.263, 3.85]]}, {"text": "Blockbuster was the king of movie nights, with almost nine thousand stores.", "start": 164.016, "end": 169.104, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "bb", "els": [{"e": "store", "x": 600, "y": 620, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "count", "x": 1340, "y": 460, "to": 9000, "at": 0.2, "end": 0.8, "size": 140, "col": "gold", "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "🏬 stores worldwide", "x": 1340, "y": 620, "size": 46, "at": 0.5, "out": [1, 0]}], "bg": "sky", "mood": "calm"}, "afx": null, "words": [["Blockbuster", 0.1, 0.725], ["was", 0.725, 0.85], ["the", 0.85, 0.938], ["king", 0.938, 1.387], ["of", 1.55, 1.65], ["movie", 1.65, 1.95], ["nights", 1.962, 2.513], ["with", 2.725, 2.875], ["almost", 2.875, 3.337], ["nine", 3.35, 3.738], ["thousand", 3.75, 4.15], ["stores", 4.162, 4.712]]}, {"text": "Netflix was a small startup that mailed DVDs in red envelopes. That year, it lost fifty-seven million dollars.", "start": 169.584, "end": 177.624, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "bb", "els": [{"e": "env", "x": 600, "y": 600, "w": 560, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "count", "x": 1340, "y": 460, "to": 57, "at": 0.4, "end": 0.85, "pre": "-$", "suf": "M", "size": 140, "col": "red", "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "lost in 2000", "x": 1340, "y": 620, "size": 44, "at": 0.7, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Netflix", 0.1, 0.525], ["was", 0.537, 0.65], ["a", 0.65, 0.7], ["small", 0.7, 1.1], ["startup", 1.113, 1.575], ["that", 1.7, 1.875], ["mailed", 1.875, 2.325], ["DVDs", 2.375, 3.263], ["in", 3.4, 3.587], ["red", 3.6, 3.8], ["envelopes", 3.812, 4.45], ["That", 4.85, 5.0], ["year", 5.013, 5.4], ["it", 5.662, 5.725], ["lost", 5.725, 6.075], ["fifty-seven", 6.088, 6.838], ["million", 6.838, 7.088], ["dollars", 7.088, 7.688]]}, {"text": "So its founders flew to Dallas, and offered to sell Netflix to Blockbuster, for fifty million dollars.", "start": 178.104, "end": 185.112, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "bb", "els": [{"e": "obj", "k": "jet", "x": 560, "y": 560, "w": 420, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "check", "x": 1340, "y": 560, "w": 620, "to": "Netflix", "amt": "$50,000,000", "at": 0.45, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["So", 0.1, 0.238], ["its", 0.237, 0.325], ["founders", 0.325, 0.725], ["flew", 0.738, 1.188], ["to", 1.2, 1.312], ["Dallas", 1.325, 2.025], ["and", 2.188, 2.362], ["offered", 2.362, 2.675], ["to", 2.675, 2.725], ["sell", 2.725, 3.075], ["Netflix", 3.075, 3.775], ["to", 3.788, 3.888], ["Blockbuster", 3.888, 4.725], ["for", 5.15, 5.363], ["fifty", 5.375, 5.775], ["million", 5.775, 6.075], ["dollars", 6.075, 6.638]]}, {"text": "According to Netflix co-founder Marc Randolph, Blockbuster's CEO was struggling not to laugh.", "start": 185.592, "end": 191.616, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "bb", "els": [{"e": "obj", "k": "samyell", "x": 520, "y": 620, "w": 420, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "letter", "x": 1340, "y": 320, "w": 680, "head": "DALLAS · 2000", "body": "Blockbuster's CEO was “struggling not to laugh.” — Marc Randolph", "at": 0.1, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["According", 0.1, 0.412], ["to", 0.425, 0.487], ["Netflix", 0.487, 1.05], ["co-founder", 1.05, 1.587], ["Marc", 1.587, 1.85], ["Randolph", 1.863, 2.5], ["Blockbuster's", 2.7, 3.363], ["CEO", 3.362, 3.912], ["was", 4.088, 4.238], ["struggling", 4.25, 4.838], ["not", 4.838, 5.038], ["to", 5.037, 5.112], ["laugh", 5.125, 5.662]]}, {"text": "The answer was no. Ten years later, Blockbuster filed for bankruptcy.", "start": 192.096, "end": 196.776, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "bb", "els": [{"e": "deal", "x": 960, "y": 420, "press": 0.2, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "store", "x": 760, "y": 790, "w": 440, "closed": true, "at": 0.55, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "stamp", "txt": "BANKRUPT 2010", "x": 1340, "y": 800, "at": 0.85, "col": "red", "sz": 70, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["The", 0.1, 0.15], ["answer", 0.15, 0.425], ["was", 0.425, 0.562], ["no", 0.575, 0.862], ["Ten", 1.262, 1.45], ["years", 1.45, 1.712], ["later", 1.712, 2.137], ["Blockbuster", 2.4, 3.025], ["filed", 3.025, 3.462], ["for", 3.462, 3.587], ["bankruptcy", 3.587, 4.312]]}, {"text": "Today, just one Blockbuster store is left, in Bend, Oregon. And Netflix is worth roughly two hundred fifty billion dollars.", "start": 197.256, "end": 205.872, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "bb", "els": [{"e": "pill", "txt": "📍 last store: Bend, Oregon", "x": 960, "y": 280, "size": 46, "at": 0.05, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "thennow", "then": "$50M", "now": "$250 BILLION", "at": 0.2, "end": 0.85, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Today", 0.087, 0.35], ["just", 0.362, 0.588], ["one", 0.6, 0.825], ["Blockbuster", 0.825, 1.438], ["store", 1.45, 1.712], ["is", 1.712, 1.825], ["left", 1.825, 2.337], ["in", 2.562, 2.7], ["Bend, Oregon", 2.712, 4.025], ["And", 4.438, 4.575], ["Netflix", 4.575, 5.15], ["is", 5.3, 5.412], ["worth", 5.412, 5.662], ["roughly", 5.713, 6.263], ["two", 6.412, 6.675], ["hundred", 6.688, 6.938], ["fifty", 6.95, 7.325], ["billion", 7.338, 7.663], ["dollars", 7.662, 8.25]]}, {"text": "Lesson three: the small idea you laugh at today might be the one that replaces you.", "start": 206.352, "end": 211.8, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "bb", "els": [{"e": "obj", "k": "samthink", "x": 520, "y": 620, "w": 460, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "card", "x": 1300, "y": 380, "w": 760, "big": "Lesson #3", "small": "The small idea you laugh at might replace you.", "at": 0.2, "col": "gold", "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Lesson", 0.087, 0.475], ["three", 0.487, 0.9], ["the", 1.387, 1.475], ["small", 1.475, 1.788], ["idea", 1.788, 2.087], ["you", 2.087, 2.237], ["laugh", 2.237, 2.562], ["at", 2.562, 2.612], ["today", 2.612, 3.037], ["might", 3.4, 3.7], ["be", 3.7, 3.812], ["the", 3.812, 3.913], ["one", 3.913, 4.213], ["that", 4.213, 4.325], ["replaces", 4.338, 4.838], ["you", 4.838, 5.075]]}, {"text": "Number three. Sunnyvale, California, February twenty oh-eight.", "start": 212.28, "end": 216.816, "spec": {"type": "map", "cam": [-98, 39, 1.0], "cam2": [-122.04, 37.37, 8], "chap": 3, "chapsub": "THE $44.6 BILLION NO", "pins": [{"at": [-122.04, 37.37], "label": "Yahoo", "col": "gold", "delay": 0.4}, {"at": [-122.12, 47.67], "label": "Microsoft", "col": "red", "delay": 0.6}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Number", 0.087, 0.3], ["three", 0.312, 0.725], ["Sunnyvale, California", 1.125, 2.712], ["February", 3.0, 3.487], ["twenty", 3.487, 3.8], ["oh-eight", 3.8, 4.175]]}, {"text": "Microsoft wanted to catch up with Google in search. So it made Yahoo an offer of forty-four point six billion dollars.", "start": 217.296, "end": 224.4, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "yahoo", "els": [{"e": "search", "x": 960, "y": 300, "w": 1100, "q": "how to catch up with google", "at": 0, "end": 0.45, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "check", "x": 960, "y": 680, "w": 760, "to": "Yahoo", "amt": "$44,600,000,000", "at": 0.5, "out": [1, 0]}], "bg": "sky", "mood": "tense"}, "afx": null, "words": [["Microsoft", 0.1, 0.737], ["wanted", 0.75, 0.95], ["to", 0.95, 0.987], ["catch", 1.0, 1.288], ["up", 1.288, 1.375], ["with", 1.375, 1.475], ["Google", 1.475, 1.8], ["in", 1.8, 1.9], ["search", 1.9, 2.487], ["So", 2.9, 3.0], ["it", 3.0, 3.05], ["made", 3.062, 3.263], ["Yahoo", 3.263, 3.738], ["an", 3.737, 3.825], ["offer", 3.837, 4.338], ["of", 4.438, 4.575], ["forty-four", 4.575, 5.237], ["point", 5.237, 5.525], ["six", 5.537, 5.85], ["billion", 5.85, 6.15], ["dollars", 6.15, 6.738]]}, {"text": "Yahoo's board said the offer substantially undervalued the company. Even when Microsoft raised it, Yahoo still wanted more.", "start": 224.88, "end": 232.896, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "yahoo", "els": [{"e": "deal", "x": 960, "y": 560, "press": 0.3, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "“substantially undervalues Yahoo”", "x": 960, "y": 300, "size": 46, "at": 0.05, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Yahoo's", 0.1, 0.463], ["board", 0.475, 0.85], ["said", 1.012, 1.238], ["the", 1.238, 1.338], ["offer", 1.375, 1.725], ["substantially", 1.725, 2.625], ["undervalued", 2.638, 3.238], ["the", 3.237, 3.3], ["company", 3.312, 3.763], ["Even", 4.175, 4.337], ["when", 4.338, 4.425], ["Microsoft", 4.425, 5.087], ["raised", 5.088, 5.5], ["it", 5.5, 5.662], ["Yahoo", 6.138, 6.612], ["still", 6.625, 6.963], ["wanted", 6.963, 7.213], ["more", 7.225, 7.65]]}, {"text": "A few months later, Microsoft walked away.", "start": 233.376, "end": 236.4, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "yahoo", "els": [{"e": "obj", "k": "jet", "x": 960, "y": 560, "w": 380, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "👋 Microsoft withdraws", "x": 960, "y": 300, "size": 50, "at": 0.3, "bg": "red", "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["A", 0.1, 0.138], ["few", 0.15, 0.3], ["months", 0.3, 0.562], ["later", 0.562, 0.875], ["Microsoft", 1.312, 1.975], ["walked", 1.975, 2.25], ["away", 2.25, 2.663]]}, {"text": "Then the financial crisis hit, Google kept growing, and Yahoo slowly faded.", "start": 236.88, "end": 241.92, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "yahoo", "els": [{"e": "chart", "kind": "crash", "x": 300, "y": 300, "w": 1320, "h": 520, "at": 0, "end": 0.95, "out": [1, 0]}]}, "afx": null, "words": [["Then", 0.1, 0.175], ["the", 0.175, 0.225], ["financial", 0.225, 0.625], ["crisis", 0.625, 1.05], ["hit", 1.05, 1.262], ["Google", 1.538, 1.95], ["kept", 1.962, 2.25], ["growing", 2.25, 2.75], ["and", 3.188, 3.337], ["Yahoo", 3.35, 3.775], ["slowly", 3.775, 4.213], ["faded", 4.213, 4.675]]}, {"text": "In twenty seventeen, Verizon bought Yahoo's main business for about four and a half billion dollars. Roughly a tenth of Microsoft's offer.", "start": 242.4, "end": 251.304, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "yahoo", "els": [{"e": "bars", "x": 380, "y": 360, "w": 1100, "end": 0.8, "rows": [["Microsoft's offer (2008)", 44.6, "green"], ["Verizon deal (2017)", 4.5, "red"]], "at": 0.1, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "pill", "txt": "≈ 1/10", "x": 1580, "y": 720, "size": 60, "at": 0.8, "bg": "red", "out": [1, 0]}], "cut": true}, "afx": null, "words": [["In", 0.087, 0.162], ["twenty", 0.163, 0.425], ["seventeen", 0.425, 1.1], ["Verizon", 1.375, 1.887], ["bought", 1.962, 2.262], ["Yahoo's", 2.275, 2.775], ["main", 2.775, 3.062], ["business", 3.075, 3.538], ["for", 3.55, 3.737], ["about", 3.737, 4.0], ["four", 4.0, 4.513], ["and", 4.638, 4.7], ["a", 4.7, 4.725], ["half", 4.725, 5.087], ["billion", 5.1, 5.387], ["dollars", 5.388, 5.95], ["Roughly", 6.35, 6.625], ["a", 6.625, 6.713], ["tenth", 6.725, 7.162], ["of", 7.175, 7.237], ["Microsoft's", 7.237, 8.0], ["offer", 8.012, 8.525]]}, {"text": "Lesson four: holding out for a better offer only works if you keep getting stronger.", "start": 251.784, "end": 257.064, "spec": {"type": "beat", "scene": "yahoo", "els": [{"e": "obj", "k": "samsad", "x": 520, "y": 620, "w": 460, "at": 0, "out": [1, 0]}, {"e": "card", "x": 1300, "y": 380, "w": 760, "big": "Lesson #4", "small": "Holding out only works if you keep getting stronger.", "at": 0.2, "col": "go